    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a67aa780903e9c05c201edca2a0aa00dc50218d3400747462e81f375c821f63f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source uses two related comparison statistics for different geometric questions: shifting and differencing the character argument functions localizes relative zero-count changes and supports noncoincidence or empty-interval conclusions, whereas the unshifted character difference records accumulated count mismatch, is sampled at zero ordinates to represent index displacement, and is then compressed through moments into a limiting distribution and an almost-all displacement statement.",
