    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_efd57233c04a474a5ce50e1f7dfbbdf6d8237e23da7017ed60437ee0b427a765",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source builds a dependency chain in which a prime-supported approximation supplies the moment scale for the shifted argument difference, the zero-counting formula transfers that fluctuation to a short-interval relative zero count, a threshold-set and Hölder argument turns the moment information into signed excursions on sets of positive measure, and a resulting count imbalance forces an adjacent-zero interval for one L-function containing no zero of the other.",
